# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres (local Docker, Neon, or any hosted provider).
# Local: docker compose up -d
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/flipcast
# Production: Neon (recommended) or any Postgres. Use the POOLED endpoint on
# serverless - a direct connection will exhaust Postgres' connection limit
# under concurrent requests. See src/db/index.ts.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@ep-xxx-pooler.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/flipcast?sslmode=require
# DATABASE_URL_POOLED=postgresql://user:pass@ep-xxx-pooler.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/flipcast?sslmode=require

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auth (Better Auth)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MUST be set in production. A weak or missing secret lets anyone forge a
# session cookie. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-32-plus-char-secret

# Canonical public URL. Used for password-reset links and as the primary
# trusted origin.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Extra origins allowed to authenticate, comma separated. No wildcards.
# Needed for local dev on other ports (3000/3100/3001/5173 and their
# 127.0.0.1 equivalents are always allowed) and for Vercel preview hostnames,
# which are not derivable from the env vars Vercel exposes.
# AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=https://flipcast.app,https://flipcast-git-main.vercel.app

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transactional email (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without these, password-reset emails are logged to stdout in development
# and dropped in production. Sign-up and sign-in do not require email.
# Use a send-only key scoped to your domain. "Forgot password?" appears only
# once RESEND_API_KEY is set.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# AUTH_EMAIL_FROM="Flipcast <noreply@yourdomain.com>"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public support address, shown in the footer and the privacy and terms pages.
# Built into the pages, so a change needs a redeploy.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@yourdomain.com
#
# Who may open /admin (launch metrics), comma separated. Everyone else gets a
# 404.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.com
#
# Large static files load from jsDelivr with a fallback to /public; set to 0
# to serve everything from the site (src/lib/asset-cdn.ts).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ASSET_CDN=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI clip picks (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Clip finding always works on the device. These add AI picks through Vercel
# AI Gateway for signed-in users, falling back to on-device picks on error.
# On Vercel the deployment authenticates itself; elsewhere set an API key.
# CLIP_FINDING_ENABLED=1
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
# AI_GATEWAY_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-5.5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Billing (optional — free tier works without any of this)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# With no STRIPE_SECRET_KEY the app is fully functional on the free tier and
# POST /api/billing/checkout returns 503 with a readable reason. Nothing
# degrades: quota, rendering and auth are unaffected.
#
# To enable paid plans:
#   1. Create two recurring prices in the Stripe dashboard (Creator, Agency),
#      monthly and yearly.
#   2. Set the key and the four price IDs below.
#   3. Point a webhook at https://<your-domain>/api/billing/webhook, subscribed
#      to: checkout.session.completed, customer.subscription.created,
#      customer.subscription.updated, customer.subscription.deleted.
#   4. Copy the signing secret into STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
#
# The webhook is the only writer of user.subscription_tier. Do not set the tier
# from the client or a plan could be bypassed from devtools.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_CREATOR_MONTHLY=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_CREATOR_YEARLY=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_AGENCY_MONTHLY=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_AGENCY_YEARLY=price_...
# Customer portal configuration (scripts/stripe-setup.mjs creates one).
# STRIPE_PORTAL_CONFIG_ID=bpc_...
#
# On the live site (VERCEL_ENV=production) paid plans need a live key
# (sk_live_ / rk_live_); test keys work on previews and locally. Set this only
# for a deliberate production-mode staging site that should accept test cards.
# STRIPE_ALLOW_TEST_MODE=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Publishing to YouTube and TikTok (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing appears in the UI until these are set; each platform turns on
# independently. Run the database migration first: npm run db:migrate
#
# Encrypts stored OAuth tokens. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# SOCIAL_TOKEN_KEY=
#
# YouTube: Google Cloud project with the YouTube Data API v3 enabled, an OAuth
# client (Web application) with this redirect URI:
#   https://<your-domain>/api/social/youtube/callback
# YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=
# YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# TikTok: developers.tiktok.com app with Login Kit and the Content Posting API
# (Direct Post), scopes user.info.basic and video.publish, redirect URI:
#   https://<your-domain>/api/social/tiktok/callback
# Until TikTok audits the app, posts can only be private ("Only me").
# TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=
# TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# Scheduling TikTok posts (TikTok's API cannot schedule): a private Vercel Blob
# store (BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN, added when the store is connected), a CRON_SECRET, and on Vercel Pro this in
# vercel.json -- on Hobby a cron this frequent makes deployments fail:
#   "crons": [{ "path": "/api/social/cron", "schedule": "*/5 * * * *" }]
# CRON_SECRET=
# SOCIAL_SCHEDULER_ENABLED=1
